Olist E-Commerce Data Analysis

Project Overview

This project explores the Brazilian Olist e-commerce dataset to identify sales trends, product category performance, customer feedback, payment preferences, and order delivery patterns.

Objectives

- Analyze monthly order trends.
- Identify top-performing product categories by revenue.
- Examine order statuses and fulfillment performance.
- Understand customer review score distributions.
- Analyze payment methods and payment values.
- Explore order delivery times.

Tools and Technologies

- Python
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Google Colab
- GitHub

Key Business Insights

1. Monthly orders: November 2017 recorded the highest order count in the analyzed data, with 7,544 orders.
2. Product categories: Beauty and health products generated the highest item revenue among the categories analyzed.
3. Order fulfillment: Most recorded orders had a delivered status, while cancellations and unavailable orders represent areas for further investigation.
4. Customer reviews: Five-star reviews were the most frequent rating in the dataset.
5. Payment methods: Credit cards accounted for the largest total payment value among the payment methods analyzed.

Visualizations

The project dashboard contains six visualizations covering monthly orders, category revenue, order status, review scores, payment methods, and delivery time.

Project Files

- "olist_business_dashboard.png" — Six-chart dashboard.
- ".ipynb" notebook — Python analysis and visualizations.

Dataset

The analysis uses the Olist Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset. Dataset source: "Kaggle — Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist" (https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce).

Conclusion

This analysis demonstrates how e-commerce data can be used to identify business trends and generate insights that support decisions about sales, customer experience, payments, and order fulfillment.
